WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.970
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:12.070
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:17.650
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:26.420
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.160
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.630
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.500
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.240
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.900
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.580
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.580 --> 00:01:01.250
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.630
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:12.270
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:17.170
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:22.410
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:32.520
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:37.260
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:41.990
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:59.000
If you're here to visit her,

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.600
she appreciates melons
much more than flowers.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.740
They're not from me.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.540
They're from Kiyotaka.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:11.150
Irises...

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.180
"The happiness of
those who believe," huh?

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.550
He always has these with him.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:22.260
What can faith alone win?

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:25.360
Rutherford...

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.460
Eyes Rutherford...

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:54.160
What are you thinking?

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.130
What am I to you guys?!

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:01.120
It is not yet the
time to discuss that...

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.370
Someday you will know.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:10.740
<i>Nothing has been resolved.</i>

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:15.840
<i>Not anything about my brother,
or them, or anything at all...</i>

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:28.830
<i>There's going to be another storm.</i>

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:35.560
"Dry Eyes"

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.800
When will Rio check
out of the hospital?

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.400
Not for quite a while.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:46.840
I see...

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.270
Rutherford...

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:54.950
When are these "even more
dangerous Hunters" coming?

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:58.710
All I know is that he will
be appearing very shortly.

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:04.190
Were you and Kanone in
contact with each other?

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:05.190
No.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:09.290
I haven't heard from him
since that day.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:12.100
Then how did you
get this information?

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.070
I received a letter one week ago.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.630
A letter, huh...

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:26.430
It was last Christmas
when he left us...

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.550
You sure are friendly.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:44.430
Did you used to belong to someone?

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.120
Hold still, now.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:50.830
There you go!

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.410
I don't know if you were
abandoned or if you ran away,

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.000
but live a strong life.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:06.180
What's that?

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.340
Dried fish.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:12.790
Is that a magic pocket or something?

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.660
Of course not.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.960
Then what is dried fish doing in it?!

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.520
For certain days.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.670
<i>What kind of days are
these "certain days"?</i>

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.540
Come to think of it, he...

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:29.700
Kanone Hilbert liked cats, huh...

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:39.010
"A cat is whimsical, proud,
and completely unraisable by people."

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.050
Rutherford.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:45.160
I should get back to Rio.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:48.060
Yes. Give her my regards.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.990
You should get home too,
before you catch a cold.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.930
"Massacre is our destiny.

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:06.480
We Blade Children are
children who must not live.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:12.140
Very shortly, even more dangerous
Hunters will appear before you.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:17.820
To exterminate the Blade Children..."

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:20.080
<i>Kanone...</i>

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:24.250
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:32.640
Oh, you're awake...

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:35.040
Who are these from?

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.210
From Kiyotaka.
Rutherford brought them just now.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:41.050
<i>Eyes-kun was here?!</i>

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:42.410
<i>You're so stupid, Kosuke-kun!</i>

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:44.420
Why didn't you wake me up?!

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.580
You wanted to see him that badly?

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.090
He's still down there.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:53.060
I needed to tell him to
bring a melon next time!

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:56.760
You'll get fat if you do
nothing but eat and sleep.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:58.390
<i>You're so stupid, Kosuke-kun!</i>

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:02.730
<i>Tell Eyes-kun that
for a Christmas present</i>

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:07.040
I want a cake from Santa Clause
and a net-patterned melon

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:08.370
instead of flowers!

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:10.840
Are you serious?

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:15.510
It might rain soon so
take him an umbrella...

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:34.300
Thanks, Patrasche...

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.830
I wish things could stay
just like this...

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:52.820
<i>Why aren't you crying, Narumi-san?</i>

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:54.920
While I do think it's a moving story,

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:56.990
I don't think it's enough to cry over.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.020
Besides, selecting tonight's
dinner is more urgent.

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:02.490
It's tough thinking up
something new every day.

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:05.330
You cruel and heartless demon!

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:06.830
Take this!

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:09.420
My deadly Hiyono Screw Punch!

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:12.970
You're horrible!

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:15.270
How dare you spoil the face
of an unmarried maiden?!

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:17.170
That's what you get for
saying things like that.

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:20.180
But it's weird that Patrasche
doesn't make you cry!

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.750
I can do whatever I want.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:24.310
Even the sky is crying!

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.420
You're so evil!

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:28.190
You bloodless and tearless demon!

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:31.190
Cold-hearted villain!
Amoeba! Human fly!

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.760
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:35.660
<i>I don't recall crying in a long time...</i>

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.180
<i>I wonder why...</i>

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.060
Maybe it's because of my brother...

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:59.540
Your mother died so suddenly.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.360
Eyes.

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:20.840
It's best to cry when you want to cry.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:23.270
I'm not that kind of child anymore.

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:28.280
We grew up together,
yet I've never seen you cry.

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:31.080
Sometimes it's good
to control your tears.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:34.250
But sooner or later it will
become natural to hold them back.

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:38.720
And eventually your heart will
stop feeling anything at all...

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.190
The more you can't cry
during difficult times,

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:42.780
the less sadness you'll feel.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:47.560
Eyes, you're too nice.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.470
So you SHOULD cry.

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:52.140
Even if you are one
of the Blade Children.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:54.610
You don't want to lose
something important to you...

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:57.340
Crying doesn't change anything.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:10:00.580
Besides, being a bloodless
and tearless demon

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:03.840
will be best when I face destiny.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:13.310
You'll be with me and cry
for me instead, won't you?

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:16.090
Yeah.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:17.560
Then that's enough.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:21.330
If you'll be with me then I won't
lose what's important to me.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:22.930
I'm sure of it...

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:25.100
Even in the pitch darkness,
if we're together,

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:28.300
we can probably continue
forward without losing our way.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:40.180
A cat suddenly jumped into the street!

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:44.250
It got run over?! The poor thing!

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:11.820
"The more you can't cry
during difficult times,

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:14.250
the less sadness you'll feel."

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:21.320
"You'll be with me and cry
for me instead, won't you?"

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:29.630
<i>I have no capacity for sadness...</i>

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:52.680
<i>You still haven't bought
Madoka-san a Christmas present?!</i>

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:55.530
Tomorrow is Christmas Eve, you know!

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:57.430
You're annoying.

00:11:57.430 --> 00:12:02.200
To a girl, Christmas Eve is the most
important day next to her birthday!

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.430
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:05.870
Let's go buy her a present right now!

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.540
I'll help you choose one!

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:09.210
Hey now!

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:10.970
What do you think of this?

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:12.340
How about this?

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:13.430
This?

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:20.820
Girls will love whatever
present you give them

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:24.420
<i>as long as you put your
heart into it, Narumi-san.</i>

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:26.290
I see.

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:36.070
Wow! This is so cute!

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:37.900
<i>Hey, Narumi-san!</i>

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:45.340
Ribbit! It's so cute!

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:02.060
As if a high school
student could afford that!

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:12.360
So beautiful...

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:18.730
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:23.750
You haven't chosen anything at all!

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:27.320
Do you even intend
to buy her a present?

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.910
<i>I just don't wanna buy what you like.</i>

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:34.760
That's perfect!

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:37.790
<i>Narumi-san! That!</i>

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:39.300
Which that?

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:41.770
That, right there! That!

00:13:41.770 --> 00:13:42.970
-Can't.
-Huh?

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:43.990
Look closely.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:49.540
There's no way I can get that.

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:55.610
How horrible...

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:59.080
I've skipped meals and worked
super hard to be helpful to you,

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:01.520
and look how I'm treated!

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.720
But I'm not surprised...

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:06.620
Not even Patrasche makes you cry!

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:10.180
You're a bloodless
and tearless demon!

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:14.130
Alright, alright. I'll do it.

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:15.770
Will that make you happy?

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:18.330
<i>You really will, Narumi-san?!</i>

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:32.610
Ayumu~! Narumi~!

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:52.370
<i>"Eyes...</i>

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:56.530
<i>Come with me..."</i>

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.280
<i>Kanone...</i>

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:01.800
<i>I'm...</i>

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:07.740
<i>I'm not an ordinary,
pitiable Blade Child!</i>

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:16.460
<i>It's too bad you couldn't get it,
Narumi-san...</i>

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:17.760
Yeah...

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:21.870
Oh! I'll have this gift-wrapped,

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:24.230
so you wait here!

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:29.940
Ugh.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:35.280
<i>Hurray, hurray, Narumi-san!</i>

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:41.720
<i>That's it! Go, Narumi-san!</i>

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:49.620
<i>You did it, Narumi-san!</i>

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:58.970
<i>Here you go. For Madoka-san.</i>

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:00.840
Yeah...

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:02.840
Well, then...

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:06.170
Thank you for the Christmas present!

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:08.750
See you tomorrow!

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:11.410
<i>Merry Christmas, Narumi-san!</i>

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:25.060
I'm home.

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:29.530
<i>Ayu-kun~!</i>

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:30.760
Welcome back!

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.430
Ow!

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:36.270
What's the big idea?

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:38.540
I thought you were gonna be late today?

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.980
But today's Christmas Eve Eve!

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:42.750
What the heck is "Eve Eve"?

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:44.680
It's the day before Christmas Eve,

00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:46.680
which makes it Eve Eve!

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:48.920
I thought it'd be nice to have
dinner with my cute brother-in-law

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:52.320
so I came home early for you!

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.320
Are you glad?

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:56.490
Stop being dumb and
take your job seriously!

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.900
Dumb?!

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:02.920
I guess you don't love your
sister-in-law after all!

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:05.270
Geez...

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:07.100
You must be pretty drunk...

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:10.510
You're such a party pooper.
You should be more cheerful!

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:11.840
What are you talking about?

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:15.680
Oh! Is that your
Christmas present to me?

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.420
You're such a good boy!

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:22.020
I'll be home late tomorrow
so let me have it today.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:24.190
Let's exchange presents!

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:26.290
Alright...

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:28.430
We can open them now, right?

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:29.480
Yeah...

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:48.210
This baby chick seems
really wet and sticky...

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:50.300
It has a sweating disorder.

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:54.720
Guess I'll fix something to eat.

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:55.920
What do you want?

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:59.490
-Roast beef!
-What?!

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:02.560
Christmas and roast beef are
synonymous with each other!

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:05.030
Alright, I'll make some.

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:08.360
Hold on a bit while
I go buy the stuff.

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:11.370
Okay, but hurry back.

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:13.670
She's sure in high spirits...

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:14.600
Hey, Ayumu.

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:17.510
Can I listen to this CD
while I'm waiting?

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:19.340
Sure, fine by me...

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:23.110
Eyes Rutherford is really
popular right now, you know...

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:36.390
<i>This piece...</i>

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:38.950
<i>It's the one my brother liked!</i>

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:02.770
Little Narumi...

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:09.250
If you're the younger
brother of Kiyotaka Narumi...

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:10.810
...then aim high.

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:01.830
<i>Madoka...</i>

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:11.610
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.610 --> 00:21:18.310
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:36.470
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:42.110
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:48.010
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:48.010 --> 00:21:54.590
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.590 --> 00:22:00.330
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:05.530
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:11.370
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.370 --> 00:22:22.980
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:28.750
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.750 --> 00:22:35.060
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:38.980 --> 00:22:41.190
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:42.720
Call of the Wild, Old Yeller.

00:22:42.720 --> 00:22:44.390
Lassie, Big Red.

00:22:44.390 --> 00:22:47.160
A Dog of Flanders.

00:22:47.160 --> 00:22:49.830
"Life is a long search for happiness.

00:22:49.830 --> 00:22:51.630
More than a risk of life,
it's a risk of heart."

00:22:51.630 --> 00:22:53.000
A poem by Hiyo Hiyo.

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:55.270
Next episode's highlight
is a cooking show

00:22:55.270 --> 00:22:58.440
<i>in which Madoka-san and
Hiyono-chan sing and dance!</i>

00:22:58.440 --> 00:23:00.070
Jingle bells! Jingle bells!

00:23:00.070 --> 00:23:02.070
On the next Spiral:
Bond of Reasoning...

00:23:02.070 --> 00:23:03.610
Overture

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:05.410
That's all for today's
Hiyono's Playhouse!

00:23:05.410 --> 00:23:07.940
Jingle bells! Jingle bells!
